\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Background and motivation. (a) shows he structure of popular MLLMs. MLLMs use encoders to extract features, project them into text space via a projector, and feed them into the LLM backbone to generate responses. The encoder and the LLM can be frozen to utilize off-the-shelf checkpoints. (b) compares the varying tendency of computational overhead and memory consumption across model layers between LLMs and the evaluated MLLM-3B. NF and FB denote the no-freeze and freeze-both, respectively. (c) shows the iteration time for training MLLM-3B using different parallel strategy planners under two frozen scenarios. MMoH1 and MMoH2 represent the parallel strategies for the respective frozen scenarios identified by the MMoH parallel strategy planner.}}{2}{}\protected@file@percent }
